# ── The island's heavy halves (wave I7) ──
# `inf island build` writes its terrain, road mesh and tile cache OUTSIDE the
# tree by default (`<checkout>/../island-build/`), which is the whole point of a
# recipe. These two entries are belt-and-braces for an author who points `--out`
# or `[source] cache` back inside it — a third of a gigabyte of build artifact
# in a source tree is not something to find out about from a push.
island-build/
samples/island/build/
# …and the UE bridge's staging directory (wave ASSET0's audit), for a stronger
# reason than size: `tools/ue-export/export.py` writes GIGABYTES of Marketplace,
# Fab and Megascans PNG whose licence for use outside Unreal is unestablished,
# and this repository is PUBLIC. Both doors now refuse a destination inside the
# checkout outright (`engine_checkout_above`); this is the belt under that
# brace, for a directory named by hand or left behind by an older tree.
ue-staging/
# …and the CI fixture's own. Its `[source] cache` is `tiles/` BESIDE the recipe,
# so `inf island build`'s default output — `cache_dir()/../project` — resolves
# INSIDE the tree for this one recipe. `island_gate` builds into a temp dir and
# never touches it; an author running the command by hand does.
samples/island-fixture/project/

